                    </div>
                    <ul>
                        <li>Write the protocol and API specs that firmware, mobile and backend teams build against before each release. Designed the backend hiring process and hired a backend engineer.</li>
                        <li>Made zero-downtime releases the default: blue-green cutovers using iptables, deploy scripts with health checks and automatic rollback, a staging environment that mirrors production, and feature flags for gradual rollouts.</li>
                        <li>Fixed the root causes of recurring outages: file-descriptor limits that blocked new threads and SSH logins, a service leaking MongoDB connections, and stale Redis connections that silently dropped messages.</li>
                        <li>Took over a manually deployed legacy stack in 2023. Replaced manual uploads over SFTP with automated CI/CD and upgraded Spring 4 on Java 8 to Spring Boot 2.7 on Java 17.</li>
                        <li>Set up centralized logging and monitoring with Grafana, Loki and VictoriaMetrics, replacing log files stored on production servers.</li>
                        <li>Administer Google Cloud (IAM, networking, storage, compute). Moved the marketing website to its own project, fully managed with Terraform, and reduced compute costs with a 3-year committed use discount.</li>
                        <li>Moved device telemetry from raw log files into ClickHouse, cutting storage by over 95% across three datasets (largest: 90 GB to 3.7 GB). Wrote the ingestion service in Go, connected to the main backend over gRPC.</li>
                        <li>Moved image data out of MongoDB into Cloud Storage with zero downtime, shrinking the database 54x (3.6 GB to 67 MB) and its memory use by 89% (4.6 GB to 500 MB). Removed redundant indexes and added targeted ones to stop full collection scans.</li>
                        <li>Connected IPv6-only cellular hubs to IPv4 backend services with in-kernel NAT64 (Jool and nftables), without adding a proxy. Added kernel-level rate limiting to drop abusive traffic before it reaches the application.</li>
                        <li>Built a Go tool for reading production logs over mutual TLS with a private certificate authority, so engineers no longer need SSH access to production.</li>
                        <li>Maintain the custom UDP protocol that hubs use to talk to the cloud, and the service behind it, built for peaks of up to 50,000 packets per second. Tuned it for low latency, from kernel packet handling to an adaptive JVM thread pool and allocation-free decoding. Leading R&amp;D on its next-generation replacement.</li>
